ing of these sites, at a distance of some 30-50 km from one another (Guojia 2006, 2007; Liu 2004), suggests that they were central nodes of small-scale polities each covering some 1,500-2,000 km2. Other evidence, such as the association of fortified sites with prestigious buildings and artifacts and specialized production activities, also supports this hypothesis (Liu 2004, pp. 104- 105; Underhill et al. 2008)." <br>In Zhengzhou there were sites during the Longshan that were 3 square kilometers at the center. Note: Don\'t know how far these sites controlled. \n                    '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1274, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 1207})
